## Fresh primary-source coverage and qualifications

All third-party fulltexts, extracts, images, and raw web responses are ignored local caches. Public receipts identify URLs, acquisition outcomes, hashes, and read extents. The complete detailed ledger is `primary-read-ledger.json`.

* **Neuenkirch–Tindel–Unterberger (NTU), journal-formatted institutional author copy.** Freshly acquired 32-page PDF, 1,211,802 bytes, SHA-256 `3f7467eea58ebf6998981bf0337a579f45ad1db1c544273eb955507fe2e55c68`. Read main statements, the analytic construction and Chen interface in Proposition 6, Remark 10, the full relevant Euler-lag proof, and the complete trapezoidal Theorem 2 proof. Proposition 6 is printed p.229; Remark 10 is p.230; Theorem 2 is p.226 with proof pp.237–240. Selected construction and lag pages were visually inspected. The established construction and canonical identification remain external inputs; this is not a formal reconstruction of all background theory. [Institutional copy](https://www.math.purdue.edu/~stindel/publication/papers-online/discretize-levy-area.pdf).
* **NTU, arXiv:0902.0497v1.** Fresh pinned PDF matches the manuscript's stated hash. Read the relevant theorem statement and separated-cell/lag argument, including printed p.12 equation (27). The journal-formatted copy retains near lags through log n in equation (29) and discards only the tail in equation (30). The note's specific v1 warning therefore must not be generalized into a journal-error claim. No exact-coefficient census or publisher-PDF byte identity was certified. [Pinned v1](https://arxiv.org/pdf/0902.0497v1).
* **Neuenkirch, Oberwolfach 2012.** Read the complete contribution on printed pp.2524–2525, including the vector observations, iterated-integral convention, historical lower-rate question, and Brownian formula. A 2012 conjecture is historical evidence, not proof of present openness. [Primary report](https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/46412?nt=1).
* **Neuenkirch–Shalaiko author text dated 14 July 2015.** The direct author-uploaded PDF returned 403, but the public author mathematical text was readable through the web tool. Read its definitions, theorem, remarks, conditional representation, and complete main proof. Theorem 1 concerns (H>1/2) and positive normalized liminf/finite limsup; Remark 5 records the Brownian optimum. This was not a publisher PDF, and equality to the 2016 journal bytes remains unverified. [Author text](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/280310281_The_maximum_rate_of_convergence_for_the_approximation_of_the_fractional_Levy_area_at_a_single_point).
* **Earlier historical context.** Freshly acquired and read Neuenkirch's complete Dagstuhl 2009 talk abstract, printed p.15. Freshly acquired Shalaiko's 156-page thesis; read the Sec.3.2 definitions and Theorem 3.3, pp.53–56, and its main proof, pp.59–63. Neither the complete thesis nor its numerical program was independently reproduced. [Dagstuhl report](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/16dagstuhl-seminar-proceedings/dsp-vol09391/DagSemProc.09391.1/DagSemProc.09391.1.pdf), [thesis](https://uacademic.info/download/file/0416U000568/dis.pdf).
* **Wu–Xiao and Xiao.** Freshly acquired both primary fulltexts. Read Wu–Xiao Theorem 2.1 and its complete pp.5–6 proof, and Xiao's spectral setup, Theorem 3.1, and published proof discussion on printed pp.173–175. They supply Gaussian projection, harmonizable representation, and localized Fourier antecedents. Xiao's proof discussion itself refers the final estimate to earlier Pitt/Kahane/Xiao work; those further bodies were not acquired. This does not turn these local-nondeterminism theorems into a verified implication of the full present area theorem. [Wu–Xiao](https://www.stt.msu.edu/~xiaoyimi/XW91.pdf), [Xiao](https://www.numdam.org/item/10.5802/afst.1117.pdf).
* **Underlying construction.** Freshly acquired the electronic journal reprint arXiv:math/0703697v2 of Unterberger's 2009 construction paper. Read the whole second-area convergence Sec.4.2, reprint pp.33–41, including Theorem 4.10 and its proof. Earlier moment/hypergeometric derivations and all 51 pages were not rereviewed. [Electronic reprint](https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0703697v2).
* **Unclosed method-access gaps.** Dickinson's 2007 primary publisher abstract was accessible, but the complete method body was not; the DOI request returned 403. The named SSRN 5031388 delivery also returned 403. Jackowski's DOI supplied only redirect HTML; public journal-OCR fragments did not supply a complete readable formula/method body. Their possible broader implications for rough fBm remain unverified, and are not excluded by this review. [Dickinson](https://doi.org/10.1080/07362990701540592), [SSRN record](https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=5031388), [Jackowski](https://doi.org/10.1016/0885-064X(91)90047-2).

The fresh focused search was bounded: three source-location queries, four rough-rate/method queries, and two underlying-construction queries, plus direct source fetches and overlapping author-text reads. No worldwide priority inference follows from a no-match result. No new, first-solution, new-general-method, or current-open claim is cleared. This is consistent with the paper's explicit UNKNOWN qualifications.

## Public wording and follow-up

The held candidate uses a simple explanation of sampled paths, an invisible quadratic witness, and a bound applying to every estimator. It preserves the full abstract, author/ORCID/date/version, exact target and hypotheses, explicit-constant reference, limitations, prior credits, DOI/PDF/support links, and concise AI disclosure. Dated internal review counts, administrative histories, and custody narratives belong in these research records rather than public article prose.

The support archive contains dated administrative statements such as “unpublished” and held readiness. The fresh Zenodo record establishes that the edition is now a publicly deposited preprint; historical support-stage wording is not current publication metadata. No external human peer review or formal certification is claimed.

**Follow-up: null.** The bounded source work does not justify advertising a precise new substantial question. Sharp constants, routine parameter changes, and sampling variants do not qualify merely because they are absent from this theorem. A substantive collaboration invitation may welcome independent verification or a meaningful extension without claiming novelty or offering authorship for endorsement. No outreach was prepared or initiated.

This lane changed only its new `sources/` and `reviews/scope/` files. It performed no Git, spreadsheet, site, deployment, release, or external-human communication operation.
 